  "body": "NodeVoice\nVOICE\nLATEST · Gemma 4 E2B — latest edge voice/room-state default\nLATEST · Gemma 4 E4B — stronger edge voice/NodeAgent model\nSTABLE · Gemma 3n E2B — older tiny everyday-device fallback\nSTABLE · Gemma 3n E4B — older everyday-device fallback\nLATEST · Ministral 3 3B — latest edge agent model\nLATEST · Ministral 3 8B — best latest laptop NodeAgent default\nPhi-4 Mini Reasoning — tiny logic-intensive model\nLFM2.5 Thinking 1.2B — ultra-fast local classifier/reasoner\nSTABLE · Llama 3.2 1B — stable tiny fallback\nSTABLE · Llama 3.2 3B — stable low-latency voice fallback\nSTABLE · Gemma 3 4B QAT — stable compact vision baseline\nSTABLE · Qwen3 4B — stable small NodeAgent fallback\nN\nTURNS\nSOURCE\nSim (scripted)\nOllama (local)\nOpenAI (live)\nIdle · listening\nlocal-first · no API keys\nWhy multi-agent voice loops get stuck — and how a shared room fixes it\n\nThree voice agents try to count together. With transcripts alone they loop on “yeah, exactly…” forever. Give them one server-authoritative room state and they count all the way up.\n\nvoice-a\nvoice-b\nvoice-c\nShared Room\nauthoritative state\nroomState\nscheduler\nclassifier\nRun the comparison\n\nRuns the bad vs. good demo side-by-side and narrates the good run aloud.\n\nCompare\nNodeAgent\nRun",
